# Phase 031 — Implement `module ... end`, `export`, and the `import X as Y` alias

Two runs. The first run added the feature to the parser, the tree-walking VM
and the module files. The second closed the gap that left behind: the bytecode VM
could not run a single one of the programs the first run introduced. A review of
the second run then found four defects in it, all now fixed; what they were and
how each was caught is below.

## What changed

### First run — the language feature

| File | Lines | What |
|---|---|---|
| src/lexer.rs | +2 −0 | `("as", TokenKind::As)` (`src/lexer.rs:57`) and the `As` variant — `as` was lexed as an identifier, so `import json as J` parsed as three statements |
| src/parser.rs | +191 −14 | `Statement::Module { name, body }` and `Statement::Export { names, all }` (`src/parser.rs:224`, `src/parser.rs:230`); `parse_module()` (`src/parser.rs:1084`) and `parse_export()` (`src/parser.rs:1123`); both added to the statement dispatch; `as` accepted as an alias keyword beside the older `to` (`src/parser.rs:560`); `module_body()` (`src/parser.rs:267`) and `module_declared_names()` (`src/parser.rs:288`) — one rule for reading a module's names whichever of the two spellings the file uses |
| src/vm.rs | +316 −17 | `Vm::declare_module()` (`src/vm.rs:522`) — the module scope, the `export` check, the published members; the `Statement::Module`/`Statement::Export` arms; the rewritten `Statement::Import` arm (`src/vm.rs:1003`) — circular-import refusal, a builtin namespace is importable, the alias is a name for the module, an import does not take over a name the program already holds; `module_aliases` / `importing` / `declared_modules` / `module_depth`; `is_module_name()`, `declare_member()`, `qualified_member()`, `call_method` resolves an alias to the module it names; `load_module` binds a module file's functions under the same `module_function` name; `set_var` writes into the module's own scope above `module_depth` |
| src/analyzer.rs | +22 −4 | `Statement::Module` analyzed in a scope of its own, `Statement::Export` a no-op; both in `collect_later_names`; an import declares the module's own name as well as its alias |
| src/formatter.rs | +19 −0 | `Statement::Module` and `Statement::Export` arms (`src/formatter.rs:380`) — `module M … export … end` round-trips through `rb format` |
| src/linter.rs | +4 −0 | `Statement::Module` arm so unused-variable tracking covers a module body (`src/linter.rs:336`) |
| src/runtime.rs | +1 −1 | `module_bindings` reads `module_body` (`src/runtime.rs:56`), so a module file written with `module … end` binds the same names as one written without |
| modules/MathUtils.rb | +25 −21 | the `module MathUtils … export all end` wrapper its header comment has described since it was written |
| tooling/vscode/syntaxes/redblue.tmLanguage.json | +1 −1 | regenerated by `rb grammar` — the shipped grammar file must list the new keyword (`tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:102`) |
| tests/module_system_test.rs | +380 | 18 new `#[test]` functions |

### Second run — the bytecode VM runs the same module programs, and the review round

| File | Lines | What |
|---|---|---|
| src/bytecode/codegen.rs | +96 | the alias goes in `IMPORT`'s second operand; `Statement::Module` compiles to `MODULE` over a block of its own; `Compiler::module_exports` emits the declaration's `EXPORT` run |
| src/bytecode/opcode.rs | +47 −4 | `Module` (byte 47) and `Export` (byte 48) added and documented; `has_aux`/`takes_constant_index`/`takes_block_index` updated |
| src/bytecode/format.rs | +28 −12 | `FORMAT_VERSION` 3 → 4 with the reasons in its own doc comment; a `module body` block kind (byte 7) |
| src/bytecode/vm.rs | +447 | `module`, `finish_module`, `module_exports`, `declare_member`, `constant_of`; `module_depth`, `declared_modules`, the frame's module fields; the `import` fixes below |
| src/bytecode/disasm.rs | +24 | the alias, and an `EXPORT`'s `not defined` marker, are named |
| src/parser.rs | +20 | `module_exports` is `pub` and sits with `module_declared_names`, so the compiler and the tree-walking VM read a module through one rule |
| src/vm.rs | +9 −20 | `module_exports` deleted (it lives in the parser now); `DeclaredModule` and `qualified_member` are `pub(crate)` so both VMs keep one definition |
| docs/BYTECODE.md | +66 −12 | version, version table, block-kind table, the two new instruction rows, how a module declaration compiles, and the import-alias rule |
| tests/bytecode_vm_test.rs | +352 | 12 new `#[test]` functions, and ten module declarations added to the generated corpus |
| tests/bytecode_test.rs | +96 −8 | the format-version and opcode-table assertions moved onto the new end of the table, plus a version-3 refusal test |
| tests/test_modules.rb | +128 −7 | 11 new Redblue `test` blocks, run on **both** VMs by the corpus differential test |

## The four review findings, and what each fix was

| # | Finding | Fix | The test that was red first |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **BLOCKER** — `IMPORT`'s second operand was used without a version bump, so a version-3 file's filler `0` would be read as `constants[0]` | `FORMAT_VERSION` 3 → 4, with the three changes listed in its doc comment and in `docs/BYTECODE.md` | `edge_a_version_3_file_is_refused_before_its_imports_name_an_alias` (`tests/bytecode_vm_test.rs`), `edge_a_version_3_file_is_refused_because_its_imports_name_no_alias` and `a_module_declaration_is_readable_only_by_the_version_that_names_it` (`tests/bytecode_test.rs`) |
| 2 | **BLOCKER** — a module declaration compiled inline, so the two VMs disagreed on every program that had one, and the corpus held none | `Opcode::Module` + `Opcode::Export` + a `module body` block, the frame and scope a declaration runs in, `module_depth` on `set_var`, `declared_modules` on `is_module_name`, and the published members on the `Name_member` names | `a_module_declaration_publishes_what_it_exports_on_both_vms` and six more `edge_*` tests, plus ten corpus programs named `module/…` that the differential test now runs on both VMs |
| 3 | **MAJOR** — `import` pushed the bound value for the trailing `STORE`, so a `constant` alias was refused on this VM and not on the other | the `STORE` is stepped over when the alias is already bound, which is the tree-walker's guard (`src/vm.rs:1061`) | `edge_modules_an_alias_that_is_a_constant_is_the_constant` in `tests/test_modules.rb`, which the corpus differential runs on both VMs |
| 4 | **MAJOR** — `modules.insert` ran before `compile_module`, and its `?` left the name behind | the name goes in the set only after the module has compiled **and** run | `edge_importing_the_same_module_twice_loads_it_once` and `edge_a_missing_module_member_is_refused_the_same_way_on_both_vms`, both reached through `tests/test_modules.rb` |

## Definition of done

| Requirement | Status |
|---|---|
| `rb run` of a file that does `import json as J` and then calls `J.parse("{}")` exits 0 and prints the parsed record | yes — `{a: 1}`, exit 0, **and the same output under `rb compile` + `rb vm`** |
| importing a name no module defines is a clean error naming the name, not a silent no-op — a test pins the message | yes — `edge_unknown_import_name_is_an_error_that_names_it` pins `Cannot find module 'NoSuchModuleAnywhere'` and that it is catchable; `edge_a_missing_module_member_is_refused_the_same_way_on_both_vms` pins the member case on both VMs |
| a module declared with `module Name … export … end` parses and `rb run` on it exits 0 | yes — `modules/MathUtils.rb` exits 0 on both VMs; `module_declaration_parses_and_runs`; and the declaration itself runs on both VMs, which is the second run's whole point |
| `modules/MathUtils.rb` gains the `module`/`export` wrapper its header comments describe, or a test explains in REPORT.md why it does not need one | yes — the wrapper is there, with `export all` |
| `edge_*`: an import of a name that shadows a local | yes — `edge_import_alias_shadowing_a_local_is_the_local` (tree-walker), `edge_modules_an_alias_shadowing_a_local_is_the_local` and `edge_modules_an_alias_that_is_a_constant_is_the_constant` (Redblue, both VMs) |
| `edge_*`: a module with nothing exported | yes — `edge_module_with_nothing_exported_binds_nothing` (tree-walker) and `edge_a_module_with_nothing_exported_binds_nothing` (both VMs) |
